  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4d66-2e1d-3ddd-5393" name="No Ranged Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Early Hominids had no ranged warfare, so they may not include Archers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b6ab-fba8-a6c7-a402" name="Early Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Early Hominids fight with fists, feet and teeth. Clubs (simple hand-held tools) work as in the normal rules. Natural weapons (the Spade suit) have no reach bonus and do not win drawn Exchanges against short weapons; if an unarmed attacker triples the foe's score, the Dominance! rule applies instead of Overpower.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="73ab-8071-a518-f201" name="Dominance!" hidden="false">
      <description>When an attack Overpowers with fists, feet and teeth, no extra wounds are caused. Instead the winner of the Exchange receives 1 Honour Point from the loser. Not used when playing against later tribes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c718-e360-b1ab-a061" name="Homo Erectus" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit may carry short weapons such as clubs instead of fists, feet and teeth. Only Characters may buy Skills.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
